    "body": "## Summary\n- expire stale `PAYMENT_REQUIRED` publications for the current user before listing recoverable publications\n- acquire a pessimistic lock per stale publication so recovery and the scheduler cannot settle the same row concurrently\n- reuse the existing idempotent `JOB_PUBLICATION_RELEASE` ledger path and existing payload cleanup\n- add regression coverage proving the stale reservation is released before active publications are returned\n\n## Why\nThe pending-publication endpoint previously filtered expired rows out of the UI without settling them. A user could therefore see no pending publication while part of the wallet remained reserved until the background expiry worker ran.\n\n## Validation\nCI must be green on the latest PR head before merge. No schema migration is required for this change.",
